cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the manuscript given under
  preferred-citation, and the repository with the git commit you used. The
  repository is unreleased and has no DOI. The code is MIT-licensed; the
  manuscripts are not (see LICENSING.md).
type: software
title: >-
  su2-yang-mills-area-law: manuscript and reproducibility materials for
  "Area law for four-dimensional SU(2) lattice Yang–Mills theory at
  beta_W < 2/3, and the limits of single-site mixing criteria"
version: draft-2026-09-28
authors:
  - family-names: Lockwood
    given-names: James M.
    affiliation: Spectrality Institute
repository-code: "https://github.com/Blaze61029dogQ-pixel/Chronomagnetics/tree/claude/su2-yang-mills-repo-1tb9ll/su2_yang_mills_area_law"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Manuscript, supplementary progress document and reproduction script for a
  Wilson-loop area law in four-dimensional SU(2) lattice Yang–Mills theory
  with Wilson action, at fixed lattice spacing, for beta_W < 2/3. The argument
  uses the Durhuus–Fröhlich slab reduction, a Wasserstein form of Dobrushin
  uniqueness, and a 1/4 Wasserstein Lipschitz bound for von Mises–Fisher laws
  on S^3. The manuscript also studies the limits of single-site mixing
  criteria. It makes no claim about the continuum limit or the continuum
  mass-gap problem. The MIT License covers the repository's code only.
keywords:
  - lattice gauge theory
  - Yang–Mills
  - SU(2)
  - area law
  - Dobrushin uniqueness
  - Wasserstein distance
  - von Mises–Fisher distribution
